    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43602" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">semper-vīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>ever-living</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res (Spiritus sanctus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 164</span></i>
			: herba, <i>the plant called also</i> aizoon,
				<i>evergreen</i>, <i>houseleek</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. Herb.
			123</span></i>.—Also, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sempervīva</span></b> ,
				ae,f., <i><span class="en">Pall. 1,
				35, 3</span></i>. —And in analogy with aizoon (Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀείζωον</span>), <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sempervīvum</span></b> , i,
				n., <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 13, 102, § 160</span></i>
			(not in Jahn).</div>
